DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  ffcclloosseeaallll()  function  closes  all  of  the calling process’s open
       streams.  Buffered output for each  stream  is  written  before  it  is
       closed (as for fffflluusshh(3)); buffered input is discarded.

       The standard streams, _s_t_d_i_n, _s_t_d_o_u_t, and _s_t_d_e_r_r are also closed.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       This  function  returns 0 if all files were successfully closed; on er‐
       ror, EEOOFF is returned.

